    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "AIDE-VELOCITY-HARNESS's centrepiece — the `check-finding-codified.mjs` Stop hook — closes the loop between *\"a CRITICAL finding was discovered\"* and *\"that class of finding can never silently recur.\"* Every CRITICAL / HIGH finding the harness's redteam or blueteam scans produce must write itself into `02-security.md` (a harness standards file) before the session can close. The next project built under the harness reads `02-security.md` and inherits the rule mechanically.\nOAP's spec spine is the authored-truth substrate AIDE approximates with markdown standards. Spec 174 ports the codification discipline to spec-spine shape: every CRITICAL / HIGH finding generated by `axiomregent`, `provenance-validator`, or `policy-kernel` must produce a spec spine entry before the session closes. The entry typically lives under a future `standards/security/` spec directory, or as a `§Constraints` section in the implicated spec — institutional memory at the substrate level, mechanically enforced.\nSpec 174 runs as a Stop hook entry registered with the spec 166 chain. Without it, a finding can land, the immediate fix can ship, and the next agent on the next project cannot benefit from the lesson.\n",
    "title": "Codification gate — every CRITICAL/HIGH finding writes itself into the spec spine before closure"
  },
